.\" $Revision: 1.3 $
.TH DRCMD 8
.SH NAME
drcmd \- Diablo program to manage a running dreaderd server
.PP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B drcmd
[
.B \-C
.I diablo.config
]
[
.I command
[
.I argument ...
]
]

.SH DESCRIPTION
.IR DrCmd
sends a command to the parent dreaderd server through its control socket
in path_run and prints the reply.  The words after the options are sent
as one command line.  Without a command,
.I drcmd
reads one command line from standard input.
.PP
The exit status is 0 when dreaderd ended its reply with a line holding a
single dot, 1 otherwise (no reply).
.PP
The following commands are available:
.PP
.B status
\- prints one line: "Connect=\fIn\fP Failed=\fIn\fP Dns=\fIpending\fP/\fIworkers\fP
Act=\fIactive\fP/\fImax\fP": connections accepted and refused since the
start, DNS lookups pending and DNS workers, and active connections against
the maximum (readerforks times readerthreads).
.PP
.B version
\- prints the dreaderd version.
.PP
.B help
\- lists the commands.
.PP
.B stats
\- prints server statistics.
.B rawstats
prints the same without pretty printing.
.B vstats
prints statistics per virtual server.
.PP
.B config
[
.I directive
[
.I value
]
]
\- without arguments, prints the current reader settings of diablo.config;
with a directive, prints that one; with a directive and a value, changes it
in the running server.  Options shown with a '*' cannot be changed while
the server is running.
.PP
.B pause
\- increments a pause counter.  While it is above zero, new connections
are refused with "400 ... Server is temporarily unavailable, please try
later".  Connections already open are not affected.
.PP
.B go
\- asks dreaderd to decrement its pause counter.  When the counter reaches
zero, dreaderd will reenable incoming connections.  Dreaderd will not allow
the counter to go negative.
.PP
.B exit
\- asks dreaderd to stop accepting connections, kill its children, and exit.
The command will not return until dreaderd has completed all operations and
then exited.
.PP
.B aexit
\- like
.BR exit ,
but returns at once instead of waiting for dreaderd to exit.
.PP
.B banlist
and
.B banconfig
\- print the current ban lists and ban settings.  Only when dreaderd was
built with READER_BAN_LISTS in lib/vendor.h (off by default).

.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-C " diablo.config"
Use this diablo.config instead of the default, to find the control
socket (path_run).

.SH "SEE ALSO"
